  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HIV/AIDS Intervention Programme (through Trocaire and CAFOD Partnership)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The original project has been designed for four OSSA branches, Addis Ababa, Nazreth, Dire Dawa and Harar. Please note that the objectives listed below are extracts from the objectives mentioned in the original proposal submitted to CRS, Cordaid and CAFOD in 2001 and they are the ones to be achieved by OSSA Harar branch in the remaining two years of project life. Production and distribution of IEC materials, however is a new objective that OSSA Harar branch suggested after having identified relevant needs.

&#xB7;	To provide home-based care and support for 50 PLWHAs.
&#xB7;	To provide home-based care and support for 100 AIDS Orphans.
&#xB7;	To enhance the capacity of 4 AACs through the provision of material and technical assistance.
&#xB7;	To organize one basic counselling training for 30 members of the community.
&#xB7;	To train 6 orphans in vocational skills.

&#xB7;	To produce and distribute IEC materials on HIV/AIDS prevention, care and support 
To assist communities in Harar to practice improved attitudinal and behavioural changes, which demonstrate an increased awareness of how to prevent HIV transmission.</narrative>
  </description>
